   "response_text": "I've got everything I need. Let me lay it out. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**Analysis of redirect handling in `httpx/_client.py`:**\n\n**(1) The `raise TooManyRedirects` line.**\nThere are two \u2014 one in the sync `_send_handling_redirects` (line 972) and one in the async one (line 1719). The question says \"the line\" singular, and both sync and async clients are referenced. Since the two are twins (line 972 sync, 1719 async), the sync/primary occurrence is **line 972**.\n\n**(2) Status codes where a redirect can switch the request method to GET.**\nFrom `_redirect_method` (lines 473\u2013494):\n- `codes.SEE_OTHER` \u2192 **303** (any method except HEAD)\n- `codes.FOUND` \u2192 **302** (any method except HEAD)\n- `codes.MOVED_PERMANENTLY` \u2192 **301** (only if method == POST)\n\nFrom `_status_codes.py`: `MOVED_PERMANENTLY = 301`, `FOUND = 302`, `SEE_OTHER = 303`. So: **301, 302, 303**.\n\n**(3) Headers removed when the method switches to GET.**\nLines 540\u2013544 in `_redirect_headers`:\n```python\nheaders.pop(\"Content-Length\", None)\nheaders.pop(\"Transfer-Encoding\", None)\n```\nSo: **Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding**.\n\n**(4) The one header removed on EVERY redirect regardless of origin or method.**\nLine 549 (unconditional, outside the branches):\n```python\nheaders.pop(\"Cookie\", None)\n```\nSo: **Cookie**. (Note: `Authorization` and `Host` only get touched when the origin changes \u2014 not unconditional.)\n\nANSWER: 972|301, 302, 303|Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding|Cookie",
